    <string name="optimized_kernel_switch">Enable optimized kernel</string>
    <string name="memory_info_details">Memory limit controls the maximum memory budget used by the Android Hashcat backend.\n\n512–1024 MB is usually the practical range on devices with limited RAM. Higher values can help some modes, but may also push Android into swap or trigger low-memory process kills.\n\nSelect Disabled to remove the custom limit and let Hashcat size memory itself.</string>
    <string name="workload_info_details">Workload controls how aggressively Hashcat schedules GPU work. It does not set the memory limit.\n\n-w 1 — low load and better responsiveness\n-w 2 — normal load\n-w 3 — high load\n-w 4 — maximum load\n\nHigher values can increase speed, but Android may become less responsive.</string>
    <string name="optimized_kernel_info_details">Optimized kernel enables Hashcat -O where the selected mode supports it.\n\nIt is often faster than the generic kernel, but can reduce the supported maximum password length or limit some generic-kernel features.\n\nLeave it disabled when compatibility is more important than speed.</string>
